# A chain of Float operations raises as soon as one step is too large to be
# finite, even though the next step would bring the value back into range:
# `big + big - big` never yields `big`. Subtle because the exact value of the
# whole expression is finite.
#= {raises: 'infinity', inputs: {big: 1e308}}
def {big} = import('inputs')
big + big - big
